                        "glosses": [
                            "The act or an instance of pondering; that which one ponders."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e88f10ed-81bb-4ed8-89d8-871c75c32cf4",
                                "sense_id": "45363cb3-a235-3ee7-b035-bef2aa7480f6",
                                "text": "Ponderances.com\nSubject: Thoughts for pondering and for having a chuckle or two.com\nRemember, amateurs built the ark. Professionals built the Titanic."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fd3779b3-e822-4a6d-8920-76c2c26103f4",
                                "sense_id": "45363cb3-a235-3ee7-b035-bef2aa7480f6",
                                "text": "[…] many other parts of life can come to fruition with a really good, concentrated, yet leisurely (enjoyment is key), pondering. […]\nMy Current Top 5 Ponderances\n(In no particular order and these can change at any time)\n1) Okay, this one is kind of common for us single gals: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "392be0d9-1748-46dc-900d-8055335ddc23",
                                "sense_id": "45363cb3-a235-3ee7-b035-bef2aa7480f6",
                                "text": "Merely pondering and then making plans with your ponderance is the key. The French writer Antoine de Saint-Exupéry said: \"A goal without a plan is just a wish.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2ee2aad5-aa52-4782-8bae-9f0d10f1636c",
                                "sense_id": "45363cb3-a235-3ee7-b035-bef2aa7480f6",
                                "text": "[…] sense of truth into the existentialist pondering the meaning of the statement. […] To reach a blissful state of knowing, an examined life of discipline and ritualistic ponderance about one's self must be lived, […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
